  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this crash. The error comes from PowerShell 7's update-notification code (UpdatesNotification.ShowUpdateNotification). That code calls String.PadRight with a negative width (-17), which is probably because the console window is very narrow when it opens. The 0x80131623 exit code is just the .NET FailFast code. The similar archived tickets (terminal#16660 and terminal#16301) are a different problem. They were an environment-variable bug in Terminal 1.18 and 1.19 that was fixed in 1.19.10302.0. This looks like a PowerShell bug, so please report it to the PowerShell repo and include your PowerShell version and window size. As a workaround, set the environment variable POWERSHELL_UPDATECHECK=Off, or use LTS or Off. That skips the update notification. You can also try starting Terminal with a wider window, or update PowerShell.\"}",
